From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 02:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] libliftoff: give planes with a settable zpos the layer's zpos

libliftoff only reads plane zpos, once, to order its allocation, and
never sets it. msm exposes several primary planes that all sit at zpos
0, so two layers on two of them are stacked by plane id, not by layer
zpos: an overlay on the lower plane ends up under the game. Where the
plane's zpos is a mutable range that holds the layer's value, set it
from the layer so the stacking follows the layers.
---
diff --git a/subprojects/libliftoff/plane.c b/subprojects/libliftoff/plane.c
index a2f637e..2f9c9df 100644
--- a/subprojects/libliftoff/plane.c
+++ b/subprojects/libliftoff/plane.c
@@ -360,7 +360,7 @@ plane_apply(struct liftoff_plane *plane, struct liftoff_layer *layer,
 	int cursor, ret;
 	size_t i;
 	struct liftoff_layer_property *layer_prop;
-	const drmModePropertyRes *plane_prop;
+	const drmModePropertyRes *plane_prop, *zpos_prop;
 
 	cursor = drmModeAtomicGetCursor(req);
 
@@ -381,8 +381,22 @@ plane_apply(struct liftoff_plane *plane, struct liftoff_layer *layer,
 	for (i = 0; i < layer->props_len; i++) {
 		layer_prop = &layer->props[i];
 		if (layer_prop->core_index == LIFTOFF_PROP_ZPOS) {
-			/* We don't yet support setting the zpos property. We
-			 * only use it (read-only) during plane allocation. */
+			/* Allocation treats plane zpos as fixed. Where a plane
+			 * lets us, also give it the layer's zpos, so planes that
+			 * tie there (msm has several primaries at 0) still stack
+			 * in layer order. */
+			zpos_prop = plane->core_props[LIFTOFF_PROP_ZPOS];
+			if (zpos_prop != NULL &&
+			    !(zpos_prop->flags & DRM_MODE_PROP_IMMUTABLE) &&
+			    drmModeGetPropertyType(zpos_prop) == DRM_MODE_PROP_RANGE &&
+			    check_range_prop(zpos_prop, layer_prop->value) == 0) {
+				ret = plane_set_prop(plane, req, zpos_prop,
+						     layer_prop->value);
+				if (ret != 0) {
+					drmModeAtomicSetCursor(req, cursor);
+					return ret;
+				}
+			}
 			continue;
 		}
 
